  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The token never enters the View",
      "items": [
        "the View may not import the SDK, call fetch or read a token — the no-restricted-imports override for **/views/** and **/app/** makes the fetch-in-a-view a lint error, not a convention",
        "the SDK owns the credential: auth, tenant, correlation, idempotency and client-info headers are interceptors, never per-call code",
        "tokens live in memory or in an httpOnly cookie; a secret shipped to the browser is public, so an API key never belongs in a bundle"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The server decides",
      "items": [
        "the {userType} route segment is an experience namespace, never a security decision — the URL never authorizes anything",
        "a permission is checked to shape the UI (can(\"leads.delete\")); the backend authorizes every request regardless of what the client renders",
        "a route guard hides or redirects for UX; the API rejects the request either way"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "401 is not 403",
      "items": [
        "401 means the session is not valid: refresh the token once and retry, then send the user to sign in again",
        "403 means the session is valid and the permission is missing — a forbidden state, never a retry",
        "the SDK normalizes { error: { code, message, requiredPermission?, correlationId } } into a typed union; the ViewModel maps each code to its own screen state and the correlation id is copyable on the error screen"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
